etc/opt/chrome/policies/managed/chrome_managed.json	T:// SYNTHETIC — not a real capture (Alex sign-off 2026-09-21)\n// Mirrors the documented Chrome Enterprise policy file schema (top-level object, one key per policy):\n// https://www.chromium.org/administrators/linux-quick-start/  and  https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/\n{\n  "HomepageLocation": "https://intranet.example.com/",\n  "HomepageIsNewTabPage": false,\n  "ShowHomeButton": true,\n  "RestoreOnStartup": 4,\n  "RestoreOnStartupURLs": ["https://intranet.example.com/", "https://wiki.example.com/"],\n  "ExtensionInstallForcelist": ["aaaabbbbccccddddeeeeffffgggghhhh;https://clients2.google.com/service/update2/crx"],\n  "ExtensionSettings": {"*": {"installation_mode": "blocked"}},\n  "PasswordManagerEnabled": false\n}\n
etc/opt/chrome/policies/recommended/chrome_recommended.json	T:// SYNTHETIC — not a real capture (Alex sign-off 2026-09-21)\n// Same schema source as chrome_managed.json (recommended level: users may override).\n{\n  "BookmarkBarEnabled": true,\n  "DefaultSearchProviderName": "Example Search"\n}\n
etc/opt/edge/policies/managed/edge_managed.json	T:// RECONSTRUCTION — hand-written from Microsoft's documented Edge policy names and Linux policy location\n// (/etc/opt/edge/policies/managed), not captured from a host:\n// https://learn.microsoft.com/deployedge/microsoft-edge-policies\n{\n  "HomepageLocation": "https://intranet.example.com/",\n  "SmartScreenEnabled": true,\n  "InPrivateModeAvailability": 1,\n  "ExtensionInstallBlocklist": ["*"]\n}\n
